This is the data publication corresponding to the paper
"Insect-Inspired Self-Motion Estimation with Dense Flow Fields-
An Adaptive Matched Filter Approach".

The Data and the written Matlab functions are ordered in three sections
(keep in mind, that all functions are written under Linux and possibly does not run under Windows):

1) Bias-test
In this section it is shown that the original Koenderink van Doorn algorithm
for self-motion estimation has a bias and a modified version not. The folder
"data_generation" has two functions. In function "bias_test_nonspherical"
the optical flow vectors are not spherically distributed. The data produced with
this function and plotted in the paper is stored in "produced_data/occluded_regions".

In function "bias_test_spherical_prop_error" the optical flow vectors are spherically
distributed, but this time the added gaussian error is proportional to each flow vector.
The data produced with this function and plotted in the paper is stored in "produced_data/proportional_error".

The function which produces the graphs is the same for both simulations and stored in
"data_analysis/graphs_bias_test".


2) Adaptive matched filter test
In the paper a new adaptive version of a commonly unadaptive matched filter was developed.
In this section the adaptive algorithm is tested against the unadaptive one.
The function "agent_in_sphere_initialization_test" shows the initialization
beavior of the adaptive algorithm. The corrssponding data produced with this function
is "produced_data/initialization". The graph is plotted with "data_analysis/
graph_agent_in_sphere_initialization".

With the function "agent_in_sphere_adaptive_matched_filter_test" two different runs are tested.
One without an added error "produced_data/without_errors" and one with an added
gaussian error "produced_data/with_errors". The plotting function for both runs are the same
"data_analysis/graph_agent_in_sphere_adaptive_matched_filter_test".

The function "agent_in_sphere_adaptive_matched_filter_many_parameter" tested the adaptive
matched filter with different update rates of the adaptation. The corresponding data
is stored in "produced_data/many_parameter". The plotting function is
"data_analysis/graph_agent_in_sphere_adaptive_matched_filter_many_parameter".


3) Illustrations
In the paper an expansion of the nearnesses with spherical harmonic function are done.
The function "spherical_harmonic_illustration" illustrate these spherical harmoninics.

In the test of the adaptive matched filter a virtuell agent flies inside a sphere. The curves
the agent takes are illustrated with "circle_curve_in_the_sphere" and "sinosodial_curve_in_the_sphere".

